miniJVM licensing
=================

Code authored for the miniJVM project is licensed under the MIT License below,
unless a file or directory says otherwise.

The Java runtime library also contains files derived from OpenJDK. Those files
retain their own notices and are licensed under:

    GPL-2.0-only WITH Classpath-exception-2.0

The Classpath Exception permits independent applications to link with the
runtime library and to be distributed under terms of the application's
author's choice. It does not remove the GPL obligations for the covered
runtime files themselves or for modifications derived from them. Distributing
compiled .class or JAR files does not by itself change their license.

Distributions of minijvm_rt.jar must include its META-INF/MIT_LICENSE, META-INF/LICENSE,
META-INF/CLASSPATH_EXCEPTION and META-INF/NOTICE files. Individual source-file
notices take precedence over this summary.

